  "title": "map-integer-type-parameter",
  "request": "Hey, the convert_parameters_to_pydantic function doesn't handle 'integer' types correctly – it falls back to string. Could you add proper int mapping for param.type == 'integer'?",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "browser_use/skills/utils.py",
      "search": "elif param_type == 'number':
			python_type = float
		elif param_type == 'boolean':
			python_type = bool
		elif param_type == 'object':
			python_type = dict[str, Any]
		elif param_type == 'array':
			python_type = list[Any]
		elif param_type == 'cookie':
			python_type = str  # Treat cookies as strings",
      "replace": "elif param_type == 'number':
			python_type = float
		elif param_type == 'integer':
			python_type = int
		elif param_type == 'boolean':
			python_type = bool
		elif param_type == 'object':
			python_type = dict[str, Any]
		elif param_type == 'array':
			python_type = list[Any]
		elif param_type == 'cookie':
			python_type = str  # Treat cookies as strings"
    }
